From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: other programs' context menu handlers

TortoiseGit installed but added nothing to the right-click menu (David's
list, item 18); nor did 7-Zip, WinRAR or "Edit with Notepad++": shell32's
item menu never loaded shellex\ContextMenuHandlers.

Now, as Windows: the handlers registered for the items' type, for every
file (*) and every file system object (AllFilesystemObjects), and for
folders (Directory, Folder) -- each once, none under Shell Extensions\
Blocked -- are created, given the folder and the items (IShellExtInit, a
data object with CF_HDROP), and add their items before Send to (command
offsets from 0x1000, clear of shell32's own). Their commands, their verbs
(by name, tried in turn) and their verbs' and help text (GetCommandString)
go back to them; HandleMenuMsg/HandleMenuMsg2 pass the menu's messages to
those that draw their items or fill submenus as they open, and the shell
view now hands its menu's messages (WM_INITMENUPOPUP, WM_DRAWITEM,
WM_MEASUREITEM, WM_MENUCHAR) to the menu while it is open.

Test: test/menuext-gate.sh (a handler of our own, menuext-dll.c, for * and
Directory; mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_MENU_HANDLERS). Real 7-Zip x64 (with 0780):
its "7-Zip" submenu is in a file's menu.
